+says a title the file has for a floating window of that app is known to be somebody else, from then on and whatever it is called later
+(`SomebodyElse`, `isKnownToBeSomebodyElse`). By its app alone it is not let in. Let in as a stranger, because many apps name a restored window a moment
+after showing it, it gives the slot back when it says that name (`giveBackTheSlot`): only where that is one move of one window that can be seen, with
+the arrangement as it was when it was let in (`LayoutTree.Place`); else nothing happens, and the owner takes the slot over when it comes. Nor is it a rival to
+a stranger who may be the owner, once every floating window of the file is back. One that was there all along is no rival but a witness: the app never
